  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The method could not be rigorously validated due to data availability constraints, meaning its accuracy remains untested against complete, ground-truth trip chains.",
      "what": "The study develops a Point of Interest (POI)-based time-geography method to estimate the locations of missing intermediate stops within trip chains. The approach combines travel survey data from Eskilstuna, Sweden, with OpenStreetMap network data to reconstruct travel patterns with higher computational efficiency than traditional time-geographic density estimation.",
      "why": "It provides a computationally efficient way to reconstruct incomplete travel surveys, allowing planners to better analyze intermediate activity patterns and mode choices even when spatial data is missing."
